{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1421 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ea7c982d515c35ff86bb00caf5900a42f6cfa1ff46790b9dd76c7785a6572712" :edb/db-before-t 1420 :edb/db-after-t 1421 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534733 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:23:38.775Z" 13194139534733 true] [17592186059508 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139534733 false] [17592186059508 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139534733 true] [17592186059508 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=-\\frac{1}{8}R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + 2y = 0; y = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1$. Or, in vector form,\n\n$$\n\\left< -2,1 \\right>\n$$" 13194139534733 false] [17592186059508 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ y=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" 13194139534733 true] [17592186059509 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=5 \\\\ x-6y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534733 true] [17592186059509 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n$-x + 5y = 5; x - 6y = 5$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534733 false] [17592186059509 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-5 \\\\ y=-10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" 13194139534733 true] [17592186059509 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{1}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - 5y =-5; y =-10\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-55\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle$." 13194139534733 false] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306349 13194139534733 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306356 13194139534733 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306369 13194139534733 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306376 13194139534733 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306390 13194139534733 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306383 13194139534733 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306403 13194139534733 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306410 13194139534733 true] [17592186059895 1017 #edb/ref 17592186056090 13194139534733 false] [17592186059895 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306363 13194139534733 true] [17592186059895 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534733 true] [17592186059895 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & 2x+4y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534733 true] [17592186059895 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x - 3y =-8; 2x + 4y = 4$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534733 false] [17592186059895 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & y=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(2)=-8\\,⇒\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=2.$" 13194139534733 true] [17592186060126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186057577 13194139534733 false] [17592186060126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306397 13194139534733 true] [17592186060126 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534733 true] [17592186060126 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139534733 true] [17592186060126 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${2x + 7y =-5; 7x + 11y =-4$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139534733 false] [17592186060126 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306350 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1089 "q-10329" 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1113 #uuid "db05c9ff-184b-5c3b-a183-c0b6e164dafc" 13194139534733 true] [17592186306349 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306351 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306352 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306353 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306354 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306355 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534733 true] [17592186306350 1041 "selection" 13194139534733 true] [175921